  "slug": "noise-quantum-01a5",
  "summary": "New preprints push sub-microsecond QEC feedback, multi-GPU decoding and FPGA decoder evaluation, alongside verified compilers and speculative execution for FTQC.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the classical stack that must keep pace with fault-tolerant quantum hardware. On decoding, Pêlagos orchestrates relay belief-propagation across multiple GPUs under real-time constraints, and a survey organizes hierarchical decoding by decoder- and code-level hierarchy, platforms and latency trade-offs. CHEQ evaluates decoders concurrently on an FPGA by geometric-skip circuit-level noise sampling, matching Stim firing rates within 0.16%. QuFrame closes the QEC loop within 1 μs through real-time Pauli frame tracking. Froq proposes safe speculative execution on live quantum states using compiler-assisted recovery contracts. A second strand addresses platform-specific compilation and control: an FPGA-based quantum data processing unit for neutral-atom arrays with NVQLink round-trip measurements, Lean-verified QCCD co-design scaling to 512 qubits, a machine-checked simulation compiler, and fidelity-predictive multi-vendor QPU scheduling.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
